# Git safety

The user owns all commits and repository-history changes.

You MUST NOT perform by initiative:

- `git commit`
- `git push`
- branch creation/switching for workflow purposes
- merge/rebase
- tags/releases
- destructive reset/clean operations

You MAY use read-only inspection such as `git status`, `git diff`, `git log` and equivalent commands.

When a phase is complete, leave the working tree ready for the user to inspect and commit manually.
